## The script is the clip

Each clip is a TypeScript file. Your agent writes it, you review it like any other code, and CI runs it as it is, with no model. The video is what CI recorded on the last push to `main`, and the lit line is the one running.

<Take base="{{clips}}" />

<details class="vc-more not-content">
  <summary><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8h10" /><path class="vc-more-v" d="M8 3v10" /></svg>Why it comes out the same every time</summary>
  <dl class="vc-facts">
    <div>
      <dt>Authored time</dt>
      <dd>The recorder moves the page's clock one frame at a time and stops it while the app waits, so no spinner reaches the video. <a href="/how-it-works/overview/">How it works</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Real input</dt>
      <dd>A real mouse moves on a planned path, so hover and press states fire. The cursor you see is drawn afterwards. <a href="/reference/dsl/">The clip DSL</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Same bytes</dt>
      <dd>Record a clip twice on one machine and you get the same file. Setup checks that before it writes your first clip. <a href="/how-it-works/determinism/">Determinism</a></dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</details>

